  "hist_multiples_note": "Trailing averages of the forward multiples, the model's equivalent of FactSet's FE_VALUATION(PE | FFEV_EBITDA, MEAN, NTM4_ROLL) averaged over -1AY/-3AY/-5AY to NOW: weekly observations (last trading day of each week, FactSet Global Prices close in USD; FactSet Estimates NTM consensus mean sampled weekly; FactSet Global Prices shares outstanding and FactSet Fundamentals FF_NET_DEBT of the latest fiscal quarter ended on or before the week) over the last five years. NTM P/E = close / NTM EPS mean; NTM EV/EBITDA = (close x shares + net debt) / NTM EBITDA mean. y1/y3/y5 = simple means of the last 52/156/260 weeks ending at as_of; n1/n3/n5 = weeks with a positive ratio in each window. Same consensus basis as the spot columns (broker-majority EPS, broker-adjusted EBITDA; net debt includes lease liabilities). Differences from the Excel formulas: weekly instead of daily sampling, and EV built from FactSet net debt rather than FactSet's own enterprise-value series (not exposed by the connector); not point-in-time restated (shares and net debt as later reported).",
  "hist_multiples_as_of": "2026-10-02",
  "hist_multiples_fetched": "2026-10-06",
  "adtv_note": "ADTV = average daily traded value over the last three months in US$ million: the mean of FactSet Global Prices daily turnover (volume x VWAP, USD) over the trading days of the window ending at price_date (equivalent to AVERAGE of P_VOLUME x XP_PRICE_VWAP day by day); product_of_averages_usd_m is the owner's Excel cross-check, P_VOLUME_AVG(-3AM,0) x AVERAGE(XP_PRICE_VWAP(0,-3AM,,,,USD)).",
  "refresh_note": "Refreshed nightly at 7:58 PM New York time by the Claude Routine 'FNAM Oracle: FactSet nightly refresh' (prompt in tools/oracle/FACTSET-PROMPT.md): prices are the latest completed session's close (the prior close for a page read the next morning), consensus as of the run date."
